From c7fac029aaa19c09f5c84258768b2aba3d131905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:09:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the errors found by the code map's checks
 (codemap/guides/systems-and-errors.md)

- Advanced Combat Odds: the BUG option "Ignore Barb Free Wins" was read as a global define
  that does not exist in getCombatOddsSpecific (always 0: free wins always applied), and with
  the opposite sense in CvGameTextMgr::setCombatPlotHelp (free wins applied only when the
  option said to ignore them). setCombatPlotHelp now reads the option once, with the sense of
  its name, and gives it to getCombatOddsSpecific (setCombatOddsIgnoreBarbFreeWins).
- CvCity::canConstruct took the building's info before its NO_BUILDING test, reading
  m_paBuildingInfo[-1] for NO_BUILDING (BarbarianCiv.py passes -1 for the granary class). The
  test now comes first, as in the original SDK.
- 21 building classes named a default building that nothing defines (16 in
  CIV4BuildingClassInfos.xml, 5 in the Guilds module); the game loaded each as NO_BUILDING and
  logged it. They now say NONE: the same classes, indices and game.
- BONUS_WOOL named TECH_WEAVING, which does not exist, as its trade technology; loading showed
  an XML error dialog and the bonus was tradeable from the start. It now says NONE: the same
  game, without the dialog.

Serves: P14
